        "original_id": "7238255a-cc8f-5f77-9574-56c2838e12a0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Rhys-Davies, Timothy Dalton, Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, Salli Richardson, Jamie Foxx, Foster & McElroy\n- Products: The Untouchables, Shōgun, Sliders, Robin of Sherwood, The Living Daylights, I, Claudius, The Great White Hype, Lean on Me, Who's That Girl, James Bond film series\n- Roles: Agent Michael Malone, Pilot Vasco Rodrigues, Professor Maximillian Arturo, King Richard I, General Leonid Pushkin, Macro, James Bond\n\nFacts:\n- John Rhys-Davies played Macro in \"I, Claudius.\"\n- John Rhys-Davies played Pilot Vasco Rodrigues in the mini-series \"Shōgun.\"\n- John Rhys-Davies played King Richard I in \"Robin of Sherwood.\"\n- John Rhys-Davies played General Leonid Pushkin in the 1987 James Bond film \"The Living Daylights.\"\n- \"The Living Daylights\" was released in 1987 as the fifteenth entry in the James Bond film series.\n- \"The Living Daylights\" was the first James Bond film to star Timothy Dalton as James Bond.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Agent Michael Malone in the 1993 remake of the 1950s television series \"The Untouchables.\"\n- John Rhys-Davies played Professor Maximillian Arturo in \"Sliders.\"\n- \"The Great White Hype\" stars Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, John Rhys-Davies, Salli Richardson, and Jamie Foxx.\n- Foster & McElroy are credited for songs in the movie soundtracks of \"The Great White Hype,\" \"Lean on Me,\" and \"Who's That Girl.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "75ef6a65-1190-51a0-a6b7-e0c1ef401d4f",
        "text": "Page: John Rhys-Davies. Sentence: He also played Agent Michael Malone in the 1993 remake of the 1950s television series \"The Untouchables\", Pilot Vasco Rodrigues in the mini-series \"Shōgun\", Professor Maximillian Arturo in \"Sliders\", King Richard I in \"Robin of Sherwood\", General Leonid Pushkin in the James Bond film \"The Living Daylights\", and Macro in \"I, Claudius\".\nPage: The Living Daylights. Sentence: The Living Daylights (1987) is the fifteenth entry in the \"James Bond\" film series and the first to star Timothy Dalton as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.\nPage: The Great White Hype. Sentence: It stars Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, John Rhys-Davies, Salli Richardson and Jamie Foxx.\nPage: Foster &amp; McElroy. Sentence: In addition to producing music for various television shows, they are also credited for songs in numerous movie soundtracks including \"The Great White Hype\", \"Lean on Me\", and \"Who's That Girl\".",
